Chapter: FwdConv2dTest
  cites AI chapter Conv2d

 Per-chapter coverage for Conv2d, which had none before this file, plus
 the gpu-cmd family reached from a chapter that cites Conv2d rather than
 GpuProxy directly.

 It does NOT pin the name collision it was written alongside. Conv2d used
 to declare its own gpu-cmd-conv2d, -group-norm, -silu and -upsample2x
 next to GpuProxy's, and a citer resolved to GpuProxy's either way -- so
 the four-argument calls below compiled identically before those four
 definitions were removed. The instrument that sees the collision is
 CDX3006, which fired on all four and is silent now. A test cannot fail
 on it, so this one does not claim to.

Section: Entry
  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let p = conv2d-params 3 8 3 1 1
    in let c = gpu-cmd-conv2d 100 50 8 16
    in let s = gpu-cmd-silu 32
    in act
      print-line-uni (format-conv2d p)
      print-line-uni ("conv2d rows=" & show (c.gpu-rows-a) & " cols=" & show (c.gpu-cols-a) & " out=" & show (c.gpu-offset-out))
      print-line-uni ("silu op=" & show (s.gpu-op) & " out=" & show (s.gpu-offset-out))
    end
  end
